WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.315
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.615 --> 00:00:08.839
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:14.775
Unit one: Making Friends. Today you will describe good friends using relative clauses with who.

4
00:00:15.075 --> 00:00:17.786
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:22.338
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:24.242
Acquaintance.

7
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.782
Acquaintance means a person you know a little, but not well.

8
00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:31.917
He is an acquaintance from my English class.

9
00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:35.517
Your turn. Say: Acquaintance.

10
00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:39.356
Acquaintance.

11
00:00:40.117 --> 00:00:40.746
Bond.

12
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.411
Bond means a strong feeling that connects people.

13
00:00:45.017 --> 00:00:47.759
Sharing hard times built a bond between us.

14
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.468
Your turn. Say: Bond.

15
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.195
Bond.

16
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.998
Trustworthy.

17
00:00:56.983 --> 00:00:59.726
Trustworthy means someone you can trust completely.

18
00:01:00.317 --> 00:01:02.815
A trustworthy friend keeps your secrets.

19
00:01:03.417 --> 00:01:06.243
Your turn. Say: Trustworthy.

20
00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.159
Trustworthy.

21
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:11.825
Loyalty.

22
00:01:12.817 --> 00:01:15.559
Loyalty means staying with and supporting someone.

23
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.126
Her loyalty means a lot to me.

24
00:01:18.717 --> 00:01:20.974
Your turn. Say: Loyalty.

25
00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:24.800
Loyalty.

26
00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:26.516
Get along.

27
00:01:27.517 --> 00:01:30.015
Get along means to have a friendly relationship.

28
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:32.930
I get along well with my classmates.

29
00:01:33.517 --> 00:01:36.053
Your turn. Say: Get along.

30
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:39.843
Get along.

31
00:01:40.583 --> 00:01:41.747
Common interest.

32
00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.620
Common interest means something two people both like.

33
00:01:46.217 --> 00:01:48.205
Football is our common interest.

34
00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:51.968
Your turn. Say: Common interest.

35
00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:56.148
Common interest.

36
00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:57.896
Reliable.

37
00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:02.102
Reliable means someone who always does what they promise.

38
00:02:02.717 --> 00:02:05.555
Dara is reliable. He is never late.

39
00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.814
Your turn. Say: Reliable.

40
00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:12.888
Reliable.

41
00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:14.674
Supportive.

42
00:02:15.683 --> 00:02:18.043
Supportive means helpful and encouraging.

43
00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:21.126
My friends were supportive before my exam.

44
00:02:21.717 --> 00:02:23.997
Your turn. Say: Supportive.

45
00:02:26.833 --> 00:02:27.904
Supportive.

46
00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:29.756
Sociable.

47
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.539
Sociable means enjoying being with other people.

48
00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.405
Sociable people make friends easily.

49
00:02:37.017 --> 00:02:39.808
Your turn. Say: Sociable.

50
00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:43.761
Sociable.

51
00:02:44.517 --> 00:02:45.495
Introvert.

52
00:02:46.483 --> 00:02:49.702
Introvert means a quiet person who enjoys time alone.

53
00:02:50.317 --> 00:02:52.537
As an introvert, I like reading at home.

54
00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.582
Your turn. Say: Introvert.

55
00:02:58.433 --> 00:02:59.388
Introvert.

56
00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:01.232
Extrovert.

57
00:03:02.217 --> 00:03:05.598
Extrovert means an outgoing person who loves company.

58
00:03:06.183 --> 00:03:09.602
My cousin is an extrovert. She talks to everyone!

59
00:03:10.217 --> 00:03:12.753
Your turn. Say: Extrovert.

60
00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:16.764
Extrovert.

61
00:03:17.517 --> 00:03:18.483
Connection.

62
00:03:19.483 --> 00:03:23.004
Connection means a relationship or link between people.

63
00:03:23.617 --> 00:03:25.814
We felt a connection on the first day.

64
00:03:26.417 --> 00:03:28.651
Your turn. Say: Connection.

65
00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.489
Connection.

66
00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:37.334
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:40.752
Visal, what makes someone a good friend?

68
00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:45.614
A good friend is someone who is trustworthy and loyal.

69
00:03:46.717 --> 00:03:49.357
I agree. Do you have a friend like that?

70
00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.834
Yes, Rithy. He's a friend who always supports me.

71
00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:56.067
How did you meet?

72
00:03:57.183 --> 00:04:03.028
We started as acquaintances, but football became our common interest. Now we have a strong bond.

73
00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:05.783
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:06.617 --> 00:04:09.568
Grammar focus: Relative clauses with who.

75
00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:11.020
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:14.041
A friend who is loyal will support you.

77
00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:17.298
I like people who share my interests.

78
00:04:18.183 --> 00:04:20.067
Rithy is the boy who helped me.

79
00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:24.197
Use 'who' for people. Use 'which' or 'that' for things.

80
00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:28.578
Be careful! Don't say: A friend which is loyal helps you.

81
00:04:30.533 --> 00:04:33.113
Say: A friend who is loyal helps you.

82
00:04:33.413 --> 00:04:35.529
Use 'who' for people, not 'which'.

83
00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:39.044
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:40.974
True Friends.

85
00:04:41.274 --> 00:04:44.283
I get along well with people who share a common interest.

86
00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.681
Some people are just acquaintances, but some become true friends.

87
00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:53.489
A trustworthy, loyal friend builds a strong connection over time.

88
00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.533
Introverts and extroverts can both be great friends.

89
00:04:58.533 --> 00:05:02.692
The best friend is someone who is supportive in good times and bad times.

90
00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:07.767
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:08.617 --> 00:05:11.023
A friend blank is loyal will support you.

92
00:05:11.323 --> 00:05:14.303
A, who. B, which. C, where.

93
00:05:17.867 --> 00:05:19.321
The answer is A: who.

94
00:05:20.483 --> 00:05:22.657
A person you know a little is an blank.

95
00:05:22.957 --> 00:05:26.425
A, acquaintance. B, extrovert. C, connection.

96
00:05:29.967 --> 00:05:31.978
The answer is A: acquaintance.

97
00:05:33.117 --> 00:05:35.766
Someone who always does what they promise is blank.

98
00:05:36.066 --> 00:05:39.430
A, reliable. B, sociable. C, shy.

99
00:05:42.967 --> 00:05:45.291
The answer is A: reliable.

100
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:49.721
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:53.163
What qualities make someone a good friend?

102
00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:03.474
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:03.774 --> 00:06:13.113
A good friend is someone who is trustworthy, reliable and supportive. My best friend is a person who listens to me when I have a problem.

104
00:06:13.413 --> 00:06:15.262
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:20.695
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and relative clauses with who.

106
00:06:20.995 --> 00:06:25.981
Today's value is loyalty. Stand by your friends in good times and bad times.

107
00:06:26.281 --> 00:06:28.701
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

108
00:06:29.001 --> 00:06:32.570
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

